{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.coventry.ac.uk/jobs/career-opportunities/": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "Opportunities | Jobs at Coventry University Group Skip to main content Skip to footer Join us | Jobs at Coventry University Group Login Search Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations Search Career Opportunities Careers home > Career Opportunities We invest in our people Coventry University Group fosters a culture of continuous learning and development. We invest in our people, and provide access to cutting-edge resources, training programmes, and professional growth opportunities. We embrace diversity and inclusivity, value unique perspectives, and recognise contributions that each individual brings. Our career opportunities enable you to collaborate with talented colleagues across our UK locations in Coventry, London, and Scarborough, as well as our international campuses and global hubs. Together, through education, we strive to transform lives and shape the future of the world. Are you ready to embark on an exciting journey and be part of an institution that empowers people and creates better futures? Take the first step towards a career at Coventry University Group and explore the job opportunities. Academic Careers In our 2030 Strategy we prioritise transformative education, investing in student engagement, educational programs, curriculum, and employability. Coventry University Group is a leading institution with a 5 QS Stars Overall Rating - QS Stars University Ratings. If you're looking for a career in academia and you're also passionate about creating better futures through education, Coventry University Group could be the perfect fit. Search academic jobs Research Careers We are an ambitious and innovative institution, and we focus on research that makes a real-world impact. Our interdisciplinary research centres tackle global challenges while upholding high standards of ethics and governance. We offer exciting career opportunities for researchers at all stages and promote partnerships and collaborations. With support in grant acquisition and a responsive research environment, we aim to create an inclusive and supportive atmosphere for researchers, celebrating past successes and striving for an even more ambitious future. Search research jobs Professional Services Coventry University Group provides high-quality assistance to students, staff, and research teams while connecting with partners and the broader community. Our focus is on delivering an exceptional educational experience, promoting core values, and embracing inclusivity. Key areas include digital services, marketing, facilities, human resources, library services, customer service, procurement and finance. Joining Professional Services means playing a pivotal role in ensuring the university's sustainability and success. Search professional jobs Apprenticeships By collaborating closely with renowned industry partners, we ensure our apprentices gain practical skills and insights that propel them towards successful careers as well as upskilling our current employees. With a focus on experiential learning, our university apprenticeship program paves the way for a new generation of well-rounded professionals, equipped with both theoretical knowledge and invaluable real-world experience. Discover apprenticeships CU Coventry CU London CU Scarborough Coventry University Coventry University London Contact us Coventry University Priory Street Coventry CV1 5FB United Kingdom Tel: +44 (0)24 7765 6565 Contact us Find us Our locations Coventry University London CU Coventry CU London CU Scarborough Coventry University Wrocław NITE Online Useful links New students News Events Student documents and verifications Library Blogs Careers Safeguarding Our staff Our organisation Complaints Follow us Sign in Student portal Staff portal The Student Contract Accessibility Copyright Statement Freedom of Information Intellectual Property Cookie Notice Website Privacy Notice Data Protection"
    },
    "https://www.coventry.ac.uk/jobs/our-culture/": {
      "title": "Our Culture",
      "description": "Our Culture | Jobs at Coventry University Group Skip to main content Skip to footer Join us | Jobs at Coventry University Group Login Search Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations Search Our Culture Careers home > Our Culture Values we live by At Coventry University Group we truly believe that societal advancement is achieved through a powerful education, but we also recognise the historical inequalities of society and are committed to a continual drive for equality and inclusion – from our perspective, access to a quality education should be a right, not a privilege. Finding solutions to real world challenges is at the heart of our curriculum, transdisciplinary research, innovation, and knowledge exchange activities. Our mission focuses on creating better futures – but we cannot do that alone. Our culture and behaviours are aligned to our mission, vision, and values, and we are clear in how people make a difference to our success. It is the difference that our people can make that matters to us and we will act with honesty and integrity, staying true to our mission and values, taking responsibility for our actions, and giving leadership to others. Collaboration We respect and value the contribution of colleagues, stakeholders, partners and communities to deliver real and beneficial impact. Determination We are here because we know we can make a difference and we won’t be deterred as we strive for success. Diversity and inclusion We harness the power and potential of the different cultures, backgrounds, abilities and experiences of our students, colleagues and partners to create opportunities for all. Innovation We welcome challenge and embrace change, delivering creative and innovative solutions. Integrity We stay true to our mission, vision, and values, taking responsibility for our actions and challenging our peers to achieve together. CU Coventry CU London CU Scarborough Coventry University Coventry University London Contact us Coventry University Priory Street Coventry CV1 5FB United Kingdom Tel: +44 (0)24 7765 6565 Contact us Find us Our locations Coventry University London CU Coventry CU London CU Scarborough Coventry University Wrocław NITE Online Useful links New students News Events Student documents and verifications Library Blogs Careers Safeguarding Our staff Our organisation Complaints Follow us Sign in Student portal Staff portal The Student Contract Accessibility Copyright Statement Freedom of Information Intellectual Property Cookie Notice Website Privacy Notice Data Protection"
    },
    "https://www.coventry.ac.uk/jobs/application-process/": {
      "title": "Application Process",
      "description": "Application Process | Jobs at Coventry University Group Skip to main content Skip to footer Join us | Jobs at Coventry University Group Login Search Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations Search Application Process Careers home > Application Process Begin your journey At Coventry University Group, we value your unique skills and talents. We believe in evaluating candidates based on their merits, creating a level playing field for all applicants. Our aim is to provide you with a seamless and user-friendly experience as you navigate through our application process. Join us in shaping the future of education and making a positive impact through your work. Begin your journey with Coventry University Group and take the next step towards a rewarding career. We look forward to receiving your application and welcoming you to our vibrant community of dedicated professionals. Find a role Find the advertisement for the role you are interested in and scroll to the bottom of the page. Apply Click on the \"Apply Now\" button located at the bottom of the advertisement. Create account If this is your first time applying for a role on our new Careers portal, you will need to create a new candidate account. To do this, follow the prompts to set up your new username and password. Candidate account Once you have set up your candidate account, you have two options to provide your information: Upload your CV: You can upload your CV, and the system will automatically pre-populate your details to create your profile. Free typing: Alternatively, you can manually type in your information without uploading a CV. Review CV Review your CV in relation to the role you are applying for. Ensure that your relevant experience, skillset, and achievements are clearly demonstrated. Also, double-check that your contact details are up to date. Supporting documents Depending on the role, we may request additional supporting documents along with your CV. If applicable, make sure to submit these documents as instructed. Submit After submitting your application, you can now access your new profile. Here, you can view and track the progress of your applications. Additionally, you have the option to set up email alerts, so you'll be among the first to hear about new opportunities that may be of interest to you. Tips before you apply These tips can help improve the quality of your application and increase your chances of success. Tailor your CV Customise your CV for the specific role you are applying for by highlighting relevant experience, skills, and achievements. This helps to make your application stand out. Update your contact details Ensure that your email address, phone number, and other contact information provided are current and accurate. This ensures that the employer can easily reach you for further communication. Submit supporting documents If the role requires additional documents such as a cover letter, certifications, or samples of your work, be sure to include them as instructed. These documents can provide further evidence of your qualifications and suitability for the role. Review before submitting Before finalising and submitting your application, carefully review your CV and supporting documents for any errors, typos, or inconsistencies. It's helpful to have a fresh pair of eyes review your application as well. Set up email alerts Take advantage of the option to set up email alerts in your profile. This way, you can stay informed about new opportunities that match your interests and be among the first to apply. Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) checks The University has a small number of job roles that require engagement in what is known as a Regulated Activity, relating to working with children or vulnerable individuals. If you are applying for a post with the Coventry University Group that does require a DBS check it will be detailed in the advert and job description and will also be made clear during interview. Learn more about DBS checks CU Coventry CU London CU Scarborough Coventry University Coventry University London Contact us Coventry University Priory Street Coventry CV1 5FB United Kingdom Tel: +44 (0)24 7765 6565 Contact us Find us Our locations Coventry University London CU Coventry CU London CU Scarborough Coventry University Wrocław NITE Online Useful links New students News Events Student documents and verifications Library Blogs Careers Safeguarding Our staff Our organisation Complaints Follow us Sign in Student portal Staff portal The Student Contract Accessibility Copyright Statement Freedom of Information Intellectual Property Cookie Notice Website Privacy Notice Data Protection"
    },
    "https://www.coventry.ac.uk/jobs/rewards-and-benefits/": {
      "title": "Rewards and Benefits",
      "description": "Rewards and Benefits | Jobs at Coventry University Group Skip to main content Skip to footer Join us | Jobs at Coventry University Group Login Search Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations Search Rewards and Benefits Careers home > Rewards and Benefits Benefits that work for you We offer a large range of industry leading rewards and benefits across Coventry University Group; each advertisement details the unique benefits on offer for each role along with our Group wide benefits. Change is in our DNA and Coventry University Group is constantly growing to succeed in our global mission to create better futures for all. We are privileged to play our part in making a difference to people’s lives and are always working on new ways to reward our staff for their hard work and dedication to improving our communities. Annual Leave We offer a minimum of 30 days plus 8 days Bank Holiday with the option to purchase an additional 5 days Pension Scheme We offer a wide range of pension schemes across the Group CU Rewards Access to discounts on a range of products and services through our staff benefits platform Electric Car Scheme Salary sacrifice scheme providing the opportunity to drive an EV/hybrid car at no upfront cost Wellbeing Support Discounted membership to our sports centre, financial education, physiotherapy, counselling and a 24/7 advice helpline LinkedIn Learning Unlimited access to a wide range of development courses through LinkedIn Development Training Organisational and professional training to upskill our employees BUPA Cash Plan We offer a voluntary scheme which gives a discounted rate for a BUPA Cash Plan Savings with Partners Nissan, Vodaphone and RAC Cycle to Work Scheme Cycle to Work scheme: offers savings on the cost of a new bike 50% off Tuition Fees Staff dependants eligible for a 50% reduction in tuition fees on Coventry University Undergraduate courses NUS Card Eligible to sign up for an NUS discount card and enjoy the perks of student discounts CU Coventry CU London CU Scarborough Coventry University Coventry University London Contact us Coventry University Priory Street Coventry CV1 5FB United Kingdom Tel: +44 (0)24 7765 6565 Contact us Find us Our locations Coventry University London CU Coventry CU London CU Scarborough Coventry University Wrocław NITE Online Useful links New students News Events Student documents and verifications Library Blogs Careers Safeguarding Our staff Our organisation Complaints Follow us Sign in Student portal Staff portal The Student Contract Accessibility Copyright Statement Freedom of Information Intellectual Property Cookie Notice Website Privacy Notice Data Protection"
    },
    "https://www.coventry.ac.uk/jobs/our-locations/": {
      "title": "Our Locations",
      "description": "Our Locations | Jobs at Coventry University Group Skip to main content Skip to footer Join us | Jobs at Coventry University Group Login Search Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations Search Our Locations Careers home > Our Locations Where we are Our aim within the Coventry University Group is to become a global enterprise and so far, we have established multiple campuses and initiatives both in the UK and internationally to achieve this. Our campuses offer unique and diverse learning experiences, each with its own benefits and opportunities. Coventry University Coventry University, located in the heart of Coventry, is a vibrant and multicultural campus with a rich educational heritage dating back to 1843. With excellent travel connections, a culture of innovation, and a commitment to professional development, joining Coventry University means becoming part of a dynamic community dedicated to excellence and growth. Search jobs Maps CU Coventry Discover CU Coventry - the cutting-edge institution in Coventry city centre offering practical, career-focused courses. With small classes and personalised learning, we provide a leading alternative to mainstream higher education. Located just a short walk from Coventry University, our campus offers a dynamic city atmosphere with a distinctive approach to teaching and learning. Search jobs Maps Coventry University London Located in the bustling financial district of the city, Coventry University London offers undergraduate and postgraduate courses. Immerse yourself in the London city experience with our central location near Liverpool Street Station. Our diverse community of students and staff from over 100 countries creates an enriching international environment. With excellent teaching and state-of-the-art facilities, we provide a real business experience for our students. Search jobs Maps CU London With two convenient locations in Dagenham and Greenwich, CU London is just a short distance from central London, where we offer career-focused courses and supported learning. Benefit from excellent links with local businesses, and study that fits around your life. Our modern campuses, including a digital campus, provide an innovative learning environment. Search jobs Maps CU Scarborough Our state-of-the-art campus in Scarborough is located just minutes away from the beautiful North Yorkshire coast. We offer vocational courses such as health, cyber security and business, and offer supported learning and small class sizes. Our goal is to provide high-quality, career-focused education for the Yorkshire region. Search jobs Maps Coventry University Wrocław Located in the stunning city of Wrocław, Poland, Coventry University Wrocław offers a unique British-style education. Study abroad opportunities at our UK campuses are also available to broaden cultural experiences and enhance employability. Since opening in 2020, we have established a thriving and dynamic learning environment, delivering exceptional experiences to our students. Search jobs Maps CU Coventry CU London CU Scarborough Coventry University Coventry University London Contact us Coventry University Priory Street Coventry CV1 5FB United Kingdom Tel: +44 (0)24 7765 6565 Contact us Find us Our locations Coventry University London CU Coventry CU London CU Scarborough Coventry University Wrocław NITE Online Useful links New students News Events Student documents and verifications Library Blogs Careers Safeguarding Our staff Our organisation Complaints Follow us Sign in Student portal Staff portal The Student Contract Accessibility Copyright Statement Freedom of Information Intellectual Property Cookie Notice Website Privacy Notice Data Protection"
    },
    "https://cugcareers.coventry.ac.uk/job/Coventry-Lecturer-%28Teaching%29-in-Diagnostic-Radiography-Cove-CV1-5FB/1370672657/": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Teaching) in Diagnostic Radiography Job Details",
      "description": "Lecturer (Teaching) in Diagnostic Radiography Job Details | coventryun We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Locations Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Faculty/Business Area All Location All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Job Title Lecturer (Teaching) in Diagnostic Radiography Job Reference 3714 Application Closing Date 18/09/2026 Division, Department CUHC CU Health and Care Limited (CUHC) ,AHP Diagnostic Radiography Salary Competitive starting salary range from £39,324 up to £44,710 (dependent on experience) with the potential to progress. A discretionary range for candidates with exceptional experience can be discussed/considered. Mode Permanent , Full Time Our Mission Coventry University Group is a global education provider dedicated to Creating Better Futures. We are driven by the belief that through education, equity, and innovation, we empower our students, people, and communities to transform their lives. A key focus of our 2030 Strategy is the ambitious growth of Coventry University Health and Care Limited to meet the local, national, and global health and care needs of the future. Our unique Group structure ensures CUHC has the agility and autonomy to push the boundaries, constantly innovating how we work, allowing for closer, consultative relationships with partners and joint ventures. Alongside our creative approach this will allow us to further develop the school, diversifying our provision at scale as we continue to widen access to our quality education, leading to rewarding careers in the health and social care sector. The Role As a Lecturer (Teaching) in diagnostic radiography you will undertake teaching and course co-ordination while supporting the development and delivery of undergraduate, and professional programmes and other core activities ensuring students have an effective learning experience. Based within the CUHC you will work closely with other academic colleagues to enrich the student learning and teaching experience to ensure, as appropriate, relevant aspects of research, enterprise and professional context are embedded in modules and courses. Duties include: Teach on modules and courses at HE levels 4-6 in relevant academic subject areas including curation, adaptation and creation of module teaching materials, delivering a variety of types of students learning sessions and supporting students as appropriate through informal and formal communication throughout teaching semesters Module leadership Prepare and deliver generic and specific formative and summative feedback. Qualifications Required Currently registered with the Health and Care Professions Council as a diagnostic radiographer Master’s degree in an appropriate subject or Honours Degree with appropriate professional qualification and/or membership A teaching qualification or acceptance of the requirement to acquire one if not already held PhD or active membership of an appropriate professional body would be advantageous Our Successful Candidate You will have demonstrable experience of successful teaching at higher education levels 4-6 in diagnostic radiography with high standards of teaching, learning and student engagement consistent with our reputation and track record as a high-quality provider of teaching and learning. Enthusiastic and self-motivated, you will have experience supporting, enhancing and engaging in an ‘active learning’ pedagogy with evidence in proactively supporting student success. As a global education provider, experience and awareness of learners’ cultural differences and expectations with the ability to effectively communicate with a wide range of people from diverse backgrounds is essential. Innovation and collaboration are key to our success, therefore the ability to work both independently and part of a wider team with the willingness to engage in flexible ways of working are key skills required for this role. If you believe you have the skills, experience and attributes required and would like to informally discuss this role further, please contact  Adam Ryder on ad7022@coventry.ac.uk All applicants need to complete the application form in full, provide a CV and cover letter detailing how they meet the person specification. The Benefits Along with a competitive salary we offer an industry leading Rewards and Benefits package which includes: Excellent Employers Pension Contribution 30 days Annual leave plus Bank Holidays New Holiday Purchase Scheme up to 5 additional days BUPA Cash Plan 50% off Tuition Fee’s for staff dependants CU Reward Scheme – Discounts across a range of High Street/ Online Retailers Cycle To Work scheme Our Culture As a global Education Group, equality, diversity, and inclusion are embedded within the fabric of our organisation and are a key focus of our core values. We harness the power and potential of the diverse cultures, backgrounds, abilities, and experiences of our students, colleagues, and partners to create opportunities for all. Full Job Description & Person Specification Click here to view the full job description and person specification We look forward to hearing from you! Please enable JavaScript Screen readers cannot read the following searchable map. Follow this link to reach our Job Search page to search for available jobs in a more accessible format. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Coventry Home View All Jobs Website Privacy Notice Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Confirm My Choices Accept All Cookies"
    },
    "https://cugcareers.coventry.ac.uk/job/Coventry-Lecturer-%28Teaching%29-in-Disaster-Management-and-Emergency-Planning-Cove-cv1-5hb/1370681157/": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Teaching) in Disaster Management and Emergency Planning Job Details",
      "description": "Lecturer (Teaching) in Disaster Management and Emergency Planning Job Details | coventryun We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Locations Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Faculty/Business Area All Location All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Job Title Lecturer (Teaching) in Disaster Management and Emergency Planning Job Reference 3579 Application Closing Date 18/09/2026 Division, Department PFL College of Engineering, Environment and Science (CEES) ,CEES School of The Environment Salary Competitive starting salary range from £39,324.00 up to £44,710.00 per annum (dependent upon experience) with the potential to progress. A discretionary range for candidates with exceptional experience can be discussed/considered. Mode Permanent , Full Time Our Mission PeoplesFuture Ltd (a sister company of Coventry University) provides a sector leading, dedicated inclusive service to Coventry University Group students supporting their successful global education experience and graduate employment outcomes. Tailoring our service to each students’ individual needs and career aspirations, we are an integral part of the student journey that starts at enrolment and continues beyond graduation. Our dedicated Lecturer (Teaching) team are subject specialists focused on delivering student education, which is active, social, applied, and inclusive within our vibrant and varied education environment. The Role As a Lecturer (Teaching) in Disaster Management and Emergency Planning you will undertake teaching and course co-ordination while supporting the development and delivery of undergraduate, postgraduate, and professional programs and other core activities ensuring students have an effective learning experience. Based within the College of Engineering, Environment and Science you will work closely with other academic colleagues to enrich the student learning and teaching experience to ensure, as appropriate, relevant aspects of research, enterprise and professional context are embedded in modules and courses. Duties include: Teach on modules and courses at HE levels 4-7 in Disaster Management and Emergency Planning, Environment and Sustainability academic subject areas including curation, adaptation and creation of module teaching materials, delivering a variety of types of students learning sessions and supporting students as appropriate through informal and formal communication throughout teaching semesters Engage appropriately in professional development and active membership of professional bodies to keep abreast of developments in relevant subject areas and to undertake professional development in support of teaching and subject knowledge and other core activities to ensure ‘authority to teach’. This will include participation in subject development and self directed learning including attendance at conferences or workshops (c. 4-6 days pa) and mandatory pedagogic CPD (c.4-6 days pa). The design, creation, moderation and quality assurance of appropriate module assessment. Assessment, marking and feedback; including coordination of marking teams for large modules, submission and upload of student marks within stipulated turn round periods and presentation at appropriate meetings and committees as required. To uphold high standards of academic integrity in all aspects of teaching, learning and assessment and to support students in this objective. To act as module leaders where required and appropriate including development of required supporting material. To take on specific course management roles as agreed with School management and course directors. Ensure that students have an effective learning experience by providing high quality academic guidance and advice and by enhancing their retention/progression and employability. Qualifications Required Master’s degree in an appropriate subject or Honours Degree with appropriate professional qualification and/or membership A teaching qualification or acceptance of the requirement to acquire one if not already held PhD or active membership of an appropriate professional body would be advantageous Our Successful Candidate You will have demonstrable experience of successful teaching at higher education levels 4-7 in Disaster Management and Emergency Planning with high standards of teaching, learning and student engagement consistent with our reputation and track record as a high-quality provider of teaching and learning. Enthusiastic and self-motivated, you will have experience supporting, enhancing and engaging in an ‘active learning’ pedagogy with evidence in proactively supporting student success. As a global education provider, experience and awareness of learners cultural differences and expectations with the ability to effectively communicate with a wide range of people from diverse backgrounds is essential. Innovation and collaboration are key to our success, therefore the ability to work both independently and part of a wider team with the willingness to engage in flexible ways of working are key skills required for this role. The Benefits Along with a competitive salary we offer an industry leading Rewards and Benefits package which includes: Excellent Employers Pension Contribution 30 days Annual leave plus Bank Holidays New Holiday Purchase Scheme Life Assurance 4x Salary BUPA Cash Plan 50% off Tuition Fees for staff dependants CU Reward Scheme – Discounts across a range of High Street/ Online Retailers Cycle To Work scheme Our Culture As a global Education Group, equality, diversity, and inclusion are embedded within the fabric of our organisation and are a key focus of our core values. We harness the power and potential of the diverse cultures, backgrounds, abilities, and experiences of our students, colleagues, and partners to create opportunities for all. Full Job Description & Person Specification Click here to view the full job description and person specification We look forward to hearing from you! Please enable JavaScript Screen readers cannot read the following searchable map. Follow this link to reach our Job Search page to search for available jobs in a more accessible format. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Coventry Home View All Jobs Website Privacy Notice Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Confirm My Choices Accept All Cookies"
    },
    "https://cugcareers.coventry.ac.uk/job/Coventry-Lecturer-%28Teaching%29-in-Low-Intensity-Psychological-Interventions-Cove-CV1-5FB/1370118657/": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Teaching) in Low Intensity Psychological Interventions Job Details",
      "description": "Lecturer (Teaching) in Low Intensity Psychological Interventions Job Details | coventryun We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Locations Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Faculty/Business Area All Location All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Job Title Lecturer (Teaching) in Low Intensity Psychological Interventions Job Reference 3715 Application Closing Date 11/09/2026 Division, Department CUHC CU Health and Care Limited (CUHC) ,CUHC Social Care, Communities and Psychological Therapies (SCCPT) Salary Competitive starting salary range from £39,324 up to £44,710 (dependent on experience) with the potential to progress. A discretionary range for candidates with exceptional experience can be discussed/considered Mode Part Time, Fixed term until 14/01/2028 Our Mission Coventry University Group is a global education provider dedicated to Creating Better Futures. We are driven by the belief that through education, equity, and innovation, we empower our students, people, and communities to transform their lives. Central to our 2030 Strategy is the ambitious growth of our School of Health and Care to meet the evolving health needs of the future locally, nationally, and globally. To enable this, our School has evolved into Coventry University Health and Care Limited. This agile, autonomous structure allows us to push boundaries and foster closer partnerships, enabling us to scale our provision and widen access to rewarding careers across the health and social care sector. The Role We are seeking to appoint a Lecturer in Low Intensity Psychological Interventions to join our current Psychological Wellbeing Practitioner (PWP) training delivery team within CU Health & Care, Coventry University. We are looking for a passionate and motivated Psychological Wellbeing Practitioner to join the team currently delivering our Graduate/Postgraduate Certificate in Low Intensity Psychological Interventions. The course sits alongside our Postgraduate Diploma in Cognitive Behavioural Therapy, and there will be opportunities to receive mentorship from staff across the curriculum area as part of the role. You will support the Associate Head of Department/Course Director and wider team members in the delivery of low intensity psychological therapies training in line with our national curricula and professional body requirements. You will also undertake teaching sessions and workshops, and the marking of clinical and academic submissions. Other responsibilities will include contributing to course quality assurance processes and assisting with module leadership activities and administration. Our Successful Candidate Applications are invited from BABCP/BPS-registered PWPs with a good understanding and working knowledge of the Low Intensity PWP role within NHS stepped-care Talking Therapies services. We are looking for applicants who share our passion for delivering a positive and inclusive training experience within which our trainees can thrive, and beyond which they can uphold the values of ethical, competent and patient-centred practitioners. Applicants will need to demonstrate significant knowledge in this area of clinical specialisation, and be committed to supporting the design and delivery of teaching that is engaging, innovative and which facilitates proficiency in low intensity cognitive behavioural assessment and intervention. Secondments from the NHS will be considered for this role, please email Vickie Presley ab6042@coventry.ac.uk in the first instance Qualifications Required •    Master’s degree in an appropriate subject OR (if from a professional practice background) a good Honors Degree and an appropriate professional qualification and/or membership •    Active membership of, and registration with, an appropriate professional body (BPS/BABCP) The Benefits Along with a competitive salary we offer an industry leading Rewards and Benefits package which includes: Excellent Employers Pension Contribution 30 days Annual leave plus Bank Holidays New Holiday Purchase Scheme up to 5 additional days Life Assurance 4x Salary BUPA Cash Plan 50% off Tuition Fees for staff dependants CU Reward Scheme – Discounts across a range of High Street/ Online Retailers Cycle To Work scheme Our Culture As a global Education Group, equality, diversity, and inclusion are embedded within the fabric of our organisation and are a key focus of our core values. We harness the power and potential of the diverse cultures, backgrounds, abilities, and experiences of our students, colleagues, and partners to create opportunities for all. Full Job Description and Person Specification Click here to view the full job description and person specification We look forward to hearing from you! Please enable JavaScript Screen readers cannot read the following searchable map. Follow this link to reach our Job Search page to search for available jobs in a more accessible format. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Coventry Home View All Jobs Website Privacy Notice Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Confirm My Choices Accept All Cookies"
